findings.evidence:
src/chat_template.rs:28-36: `let mut env = Environment::new(); env.set_unknown_method_callback(..); env.add_filter("tojson", ..); env.add_function(..); env.add_template("chat", &template)` — no `set_trim_blocks`/`set_lstrip_blocks`. minijinja-2.19.0 environment.rs:267 `pub fn set_trim_blocks(&mut self, yes: bool)` (doc: "Defaults to false") and :280 `set_lstrip_blocks`. transformers' `_compile_jinja_template` constructs `ImmutableSandboxedEnvironment(trim_blocks=True, lstrip_blocks=True, …)` and llama.cpp's minja uses the same options. The zephyr/TinyLlama template (`{% for message in messages %}
{% if message['role'] == 'user' %}
{{ '<|user|>
' + message['content'] + eos_token }}
…`) relies on it; TinyLlama is the maintainer's own SPM test checkpoint (src/tokenizer.rs:918-921) and its GGUF embeds that template.
